\description{
An \code{embeddings} object describes vector representations (embeddings) of the
regions of a structural attribute (such as paragraphs \code{p}) of a corpus, and
how to access them. It is a handle and does not necessarily hold the
vectors: For a large corpus, they are stored in Parquet files or a search
index (backends "parquet" and "faiss", not yet implemented), described by a
file \verb{_embeddings.json}. For small corpora and tests, the vectors can be
kept in memory as a \code{matrix} (backend "matrix").
}
\details{
The class inherits from the \code{corpus} class. Embeddings refer to regions of
one specific build of a corpus: Region numbers (strucs) change when a corpus
is rebuilt with a different segmentation. The validity method therefore
checks that the corpus version recorded in \verb{_embeddings.json} matches the
version of the corpus.

Search indexes are not stored in a slot, but kept in a cache within the
package (not yet implemented), so that \code{embeddings} objects can be
serialized.
}
